  ],
  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"14.1\"><mn>14.1</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a participant completes the bicycle race with an average speed of <math alttext=\"24,816\"><mn>24,816</mn>\n</math> yards per hour and <math alttext=\"1 mile  equals 1,760 yards\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1,760</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext></math>. It follows that this average speed is equivalent to <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 24,816 yards Over 1 hour EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 1 mile Over 1,760 yards EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>24,816</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mile</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1,760</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yards</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>, which yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 14.1 miles Over 1 hour EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>14.1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>miles</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>hour</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"14.1\"><mn>14.1</mn>\n</math> miles per hour.</p>",
